Ladybird locks a frame’s IOSurface read-only while it copies the frame’s
pixels on the CPU for a tab preview or a screenshot. The other engines
all lock around CPU reads of an IOSurface the same way: Chromium’s
IOSurfaceImageBacking reads under a ScopedIOSurfaceLock, Gecko’s
MacIOSurface::GetAsSurface() calls MacIOSurface::Lock() first, and
WebKit’s ImageBufferIOSurfaceBackend::getPixelBuffer() reads the pixels
only while the IOSurface is locked read-only.
